  "prompt": "How many customers have an average order value above 500 EUR? An order's value is the sum, over its order lines, of quantity times unit_price_eur minus line_discount_eur. A customer's average order value is the average over that customer's orders that have at least one line; orders with no lines do not count, and neither do guest orders, which have a missing customer_id. Return one column, n_customers. The result is a single row. Any row order is fine.",
